      "leanok": true,
      "mathlibok": false,
      "statement_uses": [],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 4,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Let $A,K$ be commutative rings with $K$ and $A$-algebra. let $B=\\{b_1,\\dots,b_n\\}$ be a set of elements in $K$. The discriminant of $B$ is defined as \\[\\Delta(B)= \\det \\left (\\begin{matrix} \\Tr_{K/A}(b_1b_1) &\\cdots& \\Tr_{K/A}(b_1b_n)\\\\ \\vdots & & \\vdots \\\\ \\Tr_{K/A}(b_nb_1) &\\cdots& \\Tr_{K/A}(b_nb_n) \\end{matrix} \\right ).\\]"
    },
    {
