      "proof_chapter": "cyclotomic-fields",
      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "Let $p$ be an odd prime, $\\zeta_p$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity and let $K=\\QQ(\\zeta_p)$. Then for any $i,j \\in {0,\\dots,p-1}$ with $i \\ne j$, there exists a unit $u \\in \\mathcal{O}_K^\\times$ such that $\\zeta_p^i-\\zeta_p^j = u (\\zeta_p-1)$."
    },
