      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "Let $p \\geq 5$ be an prime number, $\\zeta_p$ a $p$-th root of unity and $x, y \\in \\ZZ$ coprime. For $i \\neq j$ with $i,j \\in {0,\\dots,p-1}$ we can write \\[(\\zeta_p^i-\\zeta_p^j)=u(1-\\zeta_p)\\] with $u$ a unit in $\\ZZ[\\zeta_p]$. From this it follows that the ideals \\[(x+y),(x+\\zeta_py),(x+\\zeta_p^2y),\\dots,(x+\\zeta_p^{p-1}y)\\] are pairwise coprime."
    },
