      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "Let $p$ be a regular prime and let $u \\in \\ZZ[\\zeta_p]^\\times$. If $u \\equiv a \\mod p$ for some $a \\in \\ZZ$, then there exists $v \\in \\ZZ[\\zeta_p]^\\times$ such that $u=v^p$."
    },
    {
