      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": false,
      "statement_event": 74,
      "proof_event": null,
      "proof_chapter": null,
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Let $K, F$ be number fields with $F \\subseteq K$. Let $A$ be an additive subgroup of $K$. Let \\[A^{-1}=\\{ \\a \\in K | \\a A \\in \\OO_K\\}\\] and \\[A^* = \\{ \\a \\in K | \\Tr_{K/F} (\\a A) \\in \\OO_F\\}.\\] The relative different $\\gothd_{K/F}$ of $K/F$ is then defined as $((\\OO_K)^*)^{-1}$ which one checks is an integral ideal in $\\OO_K$. This is also the annihilator of $\\Omega^1_{\\OO_K/\\OO_F}$ if we want to be fancy."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:diff_ideal_eqn",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "position": 40,
      "chapter": "kummers-lemma",
      "source": "demo.tex",
      "line": 475,
      "title": null,
      "labels": [
