      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 79,
      "proof_event": 80,
      "proof_chapter": "kummers-lemma",
      "proof_leanok": false,
      "text": "Let $K$ be a number field, $p$ be a rational prime below $\\gothp$ and let $\\a_0, \\xi$ be in $\\OO_\\gothp^\\times$ (the units of the ring of integers of the completion of $K$ at $\\gothp$) be such that \\[\\a_0^p \\equiv \\xi \\mod \\gothp^{m+r}\\] where $\\gothp^m \\parallel p$ and $r(p-1)>m$. Then there exists an $\\a \\in \\OO_{\\gothp}^\\times$ such that $\\a^p =\\xi$."
    },
    {
