      ],
      "proof_uses": [],
      "has_proof": true,
      "statement_event": 81,
      "proof_event": 82,
      "proof_chapter": "kummers-lemma",
      "proof_leanok": true,
      "text": "Let $F=\\QQ(\\zeta_p)$ with $\\zeta_p$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. If $\\xi \\in \\OO_F$ and coprime to $\\lam_p:=1-\\zeta_p$ and if \\[\\xi \\equiv \\a_0^p \\mod \\lam_p^p \\] for some $\\a_0 \\in \\OO_{F_\\gothp}^\\times$ (the ring of integers of the completion of $F$ at $\\lam_p$), then the ideal $(\\lam_p)$ is unramified in $K/F$ where $K=F(\\sqrt[p]{\\xi})$."
    },
